\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  A.C. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Clark\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The Descent of Manuscripts. Oxford 1918, S. 267. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 A.C. de la Mare\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The Handwriting of Italian Humanists. Bd. 1. Oxford 1973, S. 107f., 138. \endash  S. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Caroti,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   Lo scrittoio di Bartolomeo Fonzio, umanista fiorentino (Documenti sulle arti del libro 10). Mailand 1974, S. 129. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 T. Maslowski / R.H. Rouse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Twelfth-Century Extracts from Cicero\rquote s \ldblquote Pro Archia\rdblquote  and \ldblquote Pro Cluentio\rdblquote  in Paris B.N. MS lat. 18104. In: Italia medioevale e umanistica 22, 1979, S. 110-112. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 S. Rizzo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Catalogo dei codici della Pro cluentio Ciceroniana (Pubblicazioni dell\rquote Istituto di filologia classica e medievale 75). Genua 1983, S. 80f. (Nr. 59). \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 K. Csapodin\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u233 \'e9\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  G\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u225 \'e1\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 rdonyi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Die Bibliothek des Johannes Vit\u233 \'e9z (Studia humanitatis 6). Budapest 1984, S. 97 (Nr. 31). \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 de la Mare 1985\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 529, 553. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 P.O. Kristeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Iter Italicum. Bd. 6 (Italy 3 and alia itinera 4). Supplement to Italy (G\endash V). London 1992, S. 528. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 C. Csapodi, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Bibliotheca Hungarica. Bd. 2. Budapest 1993, S. 64  (Nr. 2021). \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 F. F\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u246 \'f6\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ldesi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , in:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  A Star in the Raven\rquote s Shadow. J\u225 \'e1nos Vit\u233 \'e9z and the Beginnings of Humanism in Hungary (Ausst. Budapest), hrsg. von \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 F. F\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u246 \'f6\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ldesi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Budapest 2008, Kat. 42. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 D. Nebbiai\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , La Biblioth\u232 \'e8que du souverain et les c\u233 \'e9nacles humanistes. In: Matthias Corvin, les biblioth\u232 \'e8ques princi\u232 \'e8res et la gen\u232 \'e8se de l\rquote \u233 \'e9tat moderne (Supplementum Corvinianum II), hrsg. von \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 J.-\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 F. Maillard\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   / \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 I. Monok\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   / \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 D. Nebbiai\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Budapest 2009, S. 272f.
